+## Current bounded learnability finding: repeated colors within a segment
+
+Source SHA-256: `035e68d87137f9ace52a0763f5b739509231c260bdebfb10f7029efe4fd5ee37`.
+Selected canonical rule hash: `12836a050e75`.
+
+The ordinary generated lesson at seed 5, sample indices 0--4, default difficulty,
+has no repeated color within a blocker-separated segment in its first four
+inputs. Its fifth input has two segments with repeated colors. The plausible
+rival "left-compress each segment but keep only the first occurrence of each
+color" therefore fits all four visible demonstration labels and disagrees with
+the generated query label. All five inputs pass the current `self_check` and
+are distinct. This is a finite demonstration ambiguity, not an incorrect
+canonical label.
+
+`workspace/duplicate_color_lesson_probe.py` reproduces the finding through the
+protected Racket evaluator. One bounded run executed both programs on all five
+inputs and on a separate small constructed counterexample: 12 Racket
+applications, all assertions passed. The source and selected authority remain
+unchanged. The retained receipt and private programs/labels are in packet path
+`WORK/checks/88fc4a5c8ebd/duplicate-color-lesson/`.
+
+Proposed follow-up: guarantee a visible demonstration with repeated same-color
+values inside one blocker-separated segment, so the labels demonstrate preserved
+multiplicity as well as order. A production repair was not attempted. The
+exploratory search found this case after six seeds; this is not a prevalence
+estimate or a general identifiability guarantee. The audit did not run a full
+battery, change approval, or clear any other review state.
