+## Current bounded review: palette-dependent repetition shortcut
+
+Audited generator SHA-256:
+`71d88da03fc3c924ccb497f3adb965af74032459679fa10f93dbef73eb45e59e`.
+Canonical and generator source remain unchanged.
+
+The canonical rule always stacks two rotated copies. A plausible rival instead
+stacks one copy per distinct non-7 input color, retaining the same rotation,
+border colors, corner colors, and shared separator rows. Protected Racket
+execution shows that this rival fits all three canonical demonstrations and the
+canonical query. It therefore needs a generated palette contrast to be excluded.
+
+A bounded scan of easy seeds 0..63 found one ordinary consecutive four-input
+window exhibiting the missing contrast: seed 63, demonstrations at sample
+indices 0, 1, and 2, query at index 3. All three demonstrations contain both
+foreground colors, and the query contains one. Racket confirms that the rival
+fits every demonstration but produces a 7x8 query output where the authority
+produces 13x8. Both the original query and a smallest-declared-size 5x3 query
+pass the current generator self-check. The 5x3 query gives authoritative 9x7
+versus rival 5x7 outputs.
+
+This is a finite lesson-identifiability counterexample, not a canonical-label
+error. Proposed follow-up: ensure each three-demonstration lesson includes both
+one-foreground-color and two-foreground-color inputs, or add an executable
+palette-count rival guard. No repair or approval change was made in this review.
+
+Reproducer: `workspace/palette_copy_probe.py`.
+Packet evidence: `WORK/checks/909cd6619a84/palette-copy-v1/audit.json`, with the
+exact audited source, both programs, the complete generated lesson, and the
+minimal query under that directory's `private/` folder. The completed probe
+made 18 protected-Racket evaluations and retained program/runtime/source hashes.
+Limits: one declared rival, 64 easy seeds, no medium/hard sampling or battery;
+the candidate frequency is descriptive of this bounded scan only.
